verses.text:
When the Most High{c} handed out territories to the nations,
when he separated the human race,{d}
he set the boundaries of the peoples
to match the number of Israel’s sons.{e}

I will soak my arrows in blood,
while my sword feasts on meat,
on the blood of the dead and the prisoners,
on the heads of the enemy’s long-haired chiefs.’{l}

“Nations, sing out with joy for his people,{m}
for he will take revenge for the blood of his servants.
He will repay his enemies,
and cleanse the land and the people he loves.”{n}
